    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0524" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg456"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 184.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 11, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 183, of the 21st
                    ultimo, inviting your attention to its accompanying copy of a letter from N.
                    Mickles, esq., upon the subject of a grant which was obtained by you for the
                    East India Telegraph Company from the Chinese government, I transmit herewith,
                    for your information a copy of a <pb facs="0525" n="457" xml:id="pg457"/>
                    further communication on the subject, together with that of a circular letter
                    marked “confidential” addressed by Mr. Mickles to this department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
